{"evt":"note_created","id":"note-mqheiw4iv5t","workspace":"D:\\zonoid","title":"OVERRIDE: FeatureBench overlay/edge wiring has two bugs the SDK arms must fix","summary":"SPEC IS INCOMPLETE: the FeatureBench reference agent (.venv-fb/.../infer/agents/claude_code.py _setup_zonoid_context), which design §5 says to PORT for the canonical ON arm, has two latent bugs in its /overlay/edge wiring. Both are fixed in bench/zonoid_bench/arms.py run_canonical_wiring. (1) KIND: FB POSTs {\"from\",\"to\",\"type\":\"context\"}. The daemon (routes/overlay.js:43,51) reads b.kind, NOT b.type, so type is ignored and the edge is created as the back-compat default BLOCKING kind (it only \"works\" because a blocking edge auto-seeds a low-weight context edge via seedBlockingDepContext). Correct call: kind=\"context\" (client.overlay_edge already sends kind). (2) DIRECTION: FB wires from=note, to=node (the note CONSUMES the candidate). For a unit whose /task/context is later READ (the retrieve_and_answer executor), the KB note must be the context PROVIDER. The daemon builds a task's context_deps from edges where e.to===taskKey (depRefs, daemon.js:1599-1600; buildGraph daemon.js:1738-1740), so the provider must be `from` and the consuming unit must be `to`. Correct orientation: from=candidate(note), to=unit — identical to probe_runner.py createEdge ({\"from\":note,\"to\":probe}). FB never reads /task/context (it builds AGENTS.md from /search hits), so its reversed direction is invisible there but wrong for any DAG read. Verified live: with the corrected edge the planted note surfaces in /task/context and retrieve_and_answer returns the planted fact; with FB's orientation context_keys came back empty and the answer was \"I don't know\".","created_by":"main","valid_from":"2026-06-17T01:37:51.906Z","vec":[-0.1146676167845726,0.03560098260641098,-0.05578232184052467,0.026551123708486557,0.02211175300180912,-0.07908164709806442,0.011941744945943356,0.04617706686258316,-0.09631866961717606,0.0041